    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/ancistrus-patronus-and-ancistrus-sp-rio-tocantins/",
      "html": "<p>Ancistrus patronus is one of the numerous white dotted, black species of bristle-nose catfish. Before its scientific description in February 2019 it was known in the hobby as Ancistrus sp. “Puerto Ayacucho” and A. sp. “Rio Parucito”. The numbers L125 and L150 were given to imported animals without exact knowledge of their origin; it is assumed in catfish circles that they are also A. patronus.</p><p>A second, related form, Ancistrus sp. “Rio Tocantins”, never received an L-number, although it is very strikingly coloured. It is easily recognizable by its honeycomb pattern and occurs in nature together with the Ancistrus species L156. Apart from the different coloration, it is also much flatter than most other Ancistrus species.</p>"
    }
  ],
